{
"segments": [
{
"s": 0.84,
"e": 9.7,
"text": "Gently close your eyes and allow your sit bones to feel grounded beneath you."
},
{
"s": 10.92,
"e": 17.02,
"text": "Imagine a piece of string lightly lifting you from the crown of your head."
},
{
"s": 18.84,
"e": 28.42,
"text": "Let your shoulders soften and relax your jaw and begin by simply noticing"
},
{
"s": 28.42,
"e": 38.16,
"text": "your breathing. Notice the air entering through the nose, perhaps feeling slightly cooler as it comes in"
},
{
"s": 38.66,
"e": 46.92,
"text": "and a little warmer as it leaves. No need to change anything yet, just notice."
},
{
"s": 53.54,
"e": 57.62,
"text": "Now begin to bring a little softness into your breathing."
},
{
"s": 58.42,
"e": 69.12,
"text": "Allow the inhale to become gentle and quiet and as you exhale simply allow the air to leave."
},
{
"s": 70.96,
"e": 74.14,
"text": "No pushing, no forcing."
},
{
"s": 78.42,
"e": 88.4,
"text": "With your next breath see if you can make the inhale just a little smaller, a little softer."
},
{
"s": 89.38,
"e": 97.44,
"text": "And allow the exhale to happen naturally. Imagine there's a delicate feather resting just beneath"
},
{
"s": 97.44,
"e": 106.16,
"text": "your nose and as you breathe in and out see if you can breathe so gently that the feather"
},
{
"s": 106.16,
"e": 117.56,
"text": "barely moves. That's the quality we're looking for. Soft, quiet, imperceptible breathing."
},
{
"s": 126.82,
"e": 132.22,
"text": "Now we're going to experiment with breathing a little less air."
},
{
"s": 133.68,
"e": 140.02,
"text": "Not necessarily breathing slower but taking in a smaller amount of air with each breath."
},
{
"s": 142.09,
"e": 153.73,
"text": "Soften the inhale, relax the exhale and then see if you can soften the next inhale just a little more."
},
{
"s": 158.13,
"e": 165.67,
"text": "As you reduce the amount of air you're breathing you may begin to notice a very slight desire"
},
{
"s": 165.67,
"e": 173.89,
"text": "to take a big breath, a gentle feeling that you could do with just a little more air."
},
{
"s": 174.85,
"e": 181.67,
"text": "That's what we're exploring, just a mild comfortable sensation."
},
{
"s": 191.01,
"e": 201.23,
"text": "Continue breathing gently through your nose, a soft inhale and an effortless exhale."
},
{
"s": 202.23,
"e": 209.19,
"text": "Notice whether you can make your breathing just a little lighter, almost as though you're"
},
{
"s": 209.69,
"e": 211.77,
"text": "breathing less air than you normally would."
},
{
"s": 217.21,
"e": 224.51,
"text": "This is a bit of a dance. If you breathe too little you might feel uncomfortable."
},
{
"s": 225.79,
"e": 233.35,
"text": "If you breathe too much you may not notice any difference. See if you can find that middle ground"
},
{
"s": 234.23,
"e": 242.47,
"text": "where your breathing feels soft and relaxed with perhaps just a very slight desire for more air."
},
{
"s": 249.67,
"e": 257.55,
"text": "And remember you don't need to achieve anything here, just stay curious about what you notice."
},
{
"s": 262.43,
"e": 271.53,
"text": "And now slowly release any control over your breathing. Allow your body to breathe in whatever"
},
{
"s": 271.53,
"e": 278.45,
"text": "rhythm feels natural. No need to make the breath smaller or slower anymore."
},
{
"s": 284.03,
"e": 289.15,
"text": "Notice how you're feeling. Does your breathing feel any different?"
},
{
"s": 290.59,
"e": 298.11,
"text": "Perhaps a little quieter or more relaxed or perhaps it feels exactly the same."
},
{
"s": 299.11,
"e": 301.13,
"text": "Whatever you notice is okay."
},
{
"s": 304.91,
"e": 311.51,
"text": "When you're ready, gently bring your awareness back into the room."
}
],
